// Micro Zoom: every piece of text the player sees, in one place.
//
// How to edit: change the words between the quotes and save; nothing else
// needs to change. Keep the keys (the names before the colons) as they are,
// because the code asks for text by key: 'shell.pause.resume' is the
// `resume` line inside `pause` inside `shell` below.
//
// Placeholders in curly braces are filled in by the game; keep them, but you
// can move them around in the sentence:
//   {name}, {n}, {pct}...  a value the game fills in (a name, a number)
//   {btn:A}, {btn:Y}...    a button glyph (the A button, or its key when
//                          no controller is connected)
// A string may hold simple markup (<b>, <i>, <small>, <br>) where the game
// shows it as markup (toasts, cards, prompts); elsewhere it shows as typed.
// Choice lists in `features` map the stored value (left, keep it) to the
// words shown (right, edit freely).
//
// Another language later: copy this object into e.g. text_fr.js with the
// same keys and translated strings (keys left out fall back to English), and
// call setLocale(TEXT_FR) from shared/text.js before the page builds its
// text. The lookup helpers t() and tx() are in shared/text.js.
